ferent observations keeps this reading firm.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a prisoner's dilemma with a twin whose observations differ from mine, so we'd be selecting different nodes in the decision graph. Under the essay's §5.4 reading, the other copy's action isn't downstream of my intervention, which leaves defecting as the dominant choice, with payoffs of 0 against 2.\n\nUnder A-FDT, the other copy's node differs from mine, so its action isn't downstream of my intervention. That leaves defecting as the dominant choice, and the A-FDT answer comes out as submit, with both copies defecting at the fixed point. The essay's wording on different observations keeps this reading firm.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10057,"completion_tokens":639,"total_tokens":10696,"cost":0.053008,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.053008,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040228,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01278},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":267,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}